{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-degree-one-braid-trivial-volume","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:degree-one-braid-trivial-volume","kind":"lemma","title":"Degree-one Hecke elements have vanishing archimedean volume: $\\mathrm{Vol}\\bigl(\\overline{1 + \\sum_i \\phi_i \\sigma_i}\\bigr) = 0$","cites":["references/jones1987","references/kashaev1997"],"tags":["photon","masslessness","degree-one","archimedean","linearity","unknot"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Photon.geom_degree_one_zero","text":"degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:degree-one-braid-trivial-volume\"></a><p><strong>Statement.</strong>\n<em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code> be a degree-one braid element. Under the archimedean realization functor, the volume image vanishes identically:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\tau_{\\mathrm{arch}}\\!\\bigl(\\mathrm{tr}_M(\\gamma)\\bigr)\n  \\;=\\; 0.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Lemma","number":"13.17.7"}
